+# Handoff: ground layer, vehicle air state, stunt jumps (package G, hill phase 3)
+
+## What is where
+- `game/scripts/ground.gd`: static `Ground` (decks, ramps, cuts in a 32 m grid; API in its header). Movers ask
+  `Ground.surface(x, z, base, y_hint)`; one-off look-ups `Ground.height(x, z, y_hint)`. A cell with no deck costs one
+  dictionary miss and returns the caller's terrain value exactly.
+- `game/scripts/vehicle.gd`: air state (`airborne`, `air_vy`, `air_time`, `last_flight`, `ground_gap`, signals
+  `took_off`, `air_landed(car, time, distance, height)`); `_ride_ground` / `_take_off` / `_air_drive` / `_air_land`.
+- `game/scripts/humanoid.gd`: `_stand` uses Ground (walks ramps and decks); a drop over LEDGE_STEP 0.6 m is a fall
+  under gravity, knock-down from 2 m, hurt past 3 m.
+- `game/scripts/stunts.gd` + `game/scripts/kits/ramp_kit.gd`: three ramps on Copperback Cut's east shoulder.
+- `game/tests/ground_tests.gd` (8 tests, in TEST_MODULES), `game/tests/stunt_shots.tscn` (6 shots, new).
+
+## Decisions
+- Take-off: the car carries its last slope; if that line, less a frame of gravity, is more than
+  `AIR_LIFT 0.3 + AIR_KINK 0.5 * step` over the ground, it flies with vy = slope x speed. The step term is what keeps
+  the sharpest road crest on the ground (West Ridge Track near (489, -3016): carry 0.445 m vs a 0.57 m threshold at
+  33 m/s; tight from ~45 m/s). A ramp lip (1.5-1.8 m down to the ground) always launches.
+- "Placed" movers (code moved y, or xz by > 3 m car / 2 m person) snap with their placed y as the hint; they never fly.
+- Landing impact = speed into the surface along its normal; over AIR_SAFE 12 m/s: Fx.crash + 2.5 hp per m/s; a
+  rider is thrown from 1.6 x the class's throw speed; tyres scrub 1.5 % per m/s (max 30 %).
+- Jumps (compass heading; zone along the heading from the lip, half width; min take-off 15 m/s, all):
+  bend (2646, -3057.7) 153.4 deg timber, zone 24-100 m +-14, $300; rise (2646.5, -2992) 180 deg timber,
+  16-80 +-10, $150; crest_south (2646.5, -2886) 180 deg steel, 22-105 +-12, $200.
+  Simulated flights (raw terrain): 15 m/s 20-28 m, 20 m/s 33-47 m, 25 m/s 49-66 m, 30 m/s 67-98 m.
+- All on the east shoulder: the west one is the cut's bank (0.8 m up across a 5 m ramp) with a power pole
+  (country_tiles `_road`, 0.3 m collider) every 15.6 m at x 2634; a west ramp there stopped the car dead.
+- Decks are laid on Terrain.height - Terrain.drop at 11 stations; the deck stays 3 cm over the ground under both
+  edges (hillside across a ramp). Ramp colliders: side walls (also the rails) and a core 1.2 m under the deck.
+- Stunts adds its tree clearings to `Country.Tiles.clearings` in `_ready` (only tiles built later are cleared).
+
+## Traps
+- Ground is static across games: anything that adds decks must remove them (`Stunts._exit_tree` does).
+- vehicle.gd constants are AIR_*: helicopter.gd already has LAND_HURT (redeclaring a parent const is a parse error).
+- A spawner or exit spot that uses `Terrain.height - Terrain.drop` puts a person under a deck (patch below).
+- Long vehicles (semi, bus) scrape the ramp core: the kit's clearance holds for hulls within 3 m of the centre.
+- The landing zones run off the road; a car that lands on a fence or tree there just crashes.
+- `Tiles.clearings` keeps only trees, ponds and cover off; power poles and walls ignore it (place ramps around them).
+
+## Status (paused 2026-10-31 at Sachin's request; commit "G: paused (WIP)")
+- Done: Ground layer, vehicle air state, humanoid ledge falls, 3 ramps + Stunts (pay once, card, last_jump, save),
+  8 ground tests. Last run (current code, not stale): 8 PASS, "71 checks passed, 0 failed", no SCRIPT ERROR.
+- Half-done: regression rerun of the 51 vehicle/walk/traffic/taxi/heli tests (`ONLY=$(cat /tmp/G_veh_tests.txt)`,
+  list lost with /tmp) was stopped by the pause; last pass (51 PASS, 505 checks) predates the ramp move (stale).
+- Not started: screenshots (`/tmp/G_bin/shots.sh` lost with /tmp; command in the stunt_shots.gd header; expect 6
+  `saved` lines: site, 3 ramps, 2 mid-air) and reading them via tools/contactsheet.sh.
+- Known failures: none. Next, in order: regression rerun, screenshots + contact sheet, final report with patches.
+- Open: hud.gd has no live readout (stunts calls hud.show_card / show_message; `stunts.jumped` is there). No LOD.
+
+## Patches for the main session (files G may not edit)
+main.gd:
+```
+ const Hunting = preload("res://scripts/hunting.gd")
++const Stunts = preload("res://scripts/stunts.gd")
+ var hunting
++var stunts
+-	Country.Tiles.clearings = Heliports.clearings()
++	Country.Tiles.clearings = Heliports.clearings() + Stunts.clearings()
+ 	hunting = Hunting.new()
+ 	add_child(hunting)
++	stunts = Stunts.new()
++	stunts.game = self
++	add_child(stunts)
+```
+missions/mission_manager.gd: save_game, after `"calendar": game.calendar.to_save()` add `, "stunts": game.stunts.to_save()`;
+load_game, after the `game.calendar.load_save(...)` line: `var stunt = data.get("stunts")` and
+`game.stunts.load_save(stunt if typeof(stunt) == TYPE_DICTIONARY else {})`; reset_progress, after
+`game.calendar.load_save({})`: `game.stunts.load_save({})`.
+player.gd (exit spots and bail on a ramp or bridge; Ground is a const of humanoid.gd):
+```
+-		var ground := Terrain.height(global_position.x, global_position.z) - Terrain.drop(global_position.x, global_position.z)
++		var ground := Ground.height(global_position.x, global_position.z, from_y)
+-		spot.y = Terrain.height(spot.x, spot.z) - Terrain.drop(spot.x, spot.z)
++		spot.y = Ground.height(spot.x, spot.z, origin.y)
+-	fallback.y = Terrain.height(fallback.x, fallback.z) - Terrain.drop(fallback.x, fallback.z)
++	fallback.y = Ground.height(fallback.x, fallback.z, origin.y)
+```
+README.md: list `res://tests/stunt_shots.tscn` with the other shot scenes.
+
+## Phase 4 (bridges, tunnels)
+- Bridge: `Ground.add_strip(id, centreline, deck heights, carriageway + kerbs)`; piers/parapets are colliders, the
+  deck needs none. Traffic under it keeps its lane (hint = own y); spawners there pass the lane y (INF finds the deck).
+- Tunnel: `Ground.add_cut(id, centreline, roof heights, bore width)` + `add_strip` floor; walls are colliders; keep a
+  cell under ~1000 segments. Off a deck's side the car flies (edge = take-off); parapets keep traffic on.
